  "query_preview": "(Sunday through Wednesday)...\nThe cooling trend will continue into early next week, but with\nincreasing spread in the temperature guidance after Monday. High\ntemperatures and low temperatures on Monday will be a few degrees\nbelow average with high temperatures on Monday ranging from the\nmid 70s to lower 80s near the coast to the 90s for the Inland\nEmpire with 104 to 108 for the lower deserts.\n\nFor Tuesday and Wednesday, there could be an increase in clouds\nand a chance of precipitation from a tropical system that has yet\nto develop. The center of that possible tropical system would\nremain well to the southwest of the area, but a low pressure \nsystem near the West Coast could direct some mid and high level\nmoisture and clouds from that possible tropical system toward the\nnortheast and toward California.",
